<title>GERMANY: Wayss in 450 mln dmk Swiss tunnel contract.</title>
<headline>Wayss in 450 mln dmk Swiss tunnel contract.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German building group Wayss &amp; Freytag said on Monday it had won part of a 450 million mark ($266 million) contract to build a rail tunnel connecting the Swiss towns of Zurich and Thalwil.</p>
<p>Wayss said the nine-kilometre tunnel was part of the Swiss railways SBB &quot;Bahn 2000&quot; building programme. It said it was sharing the contract with an unnamed Swiss consortium and gave no details on its part of the contract.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.691 German Marks)</p>
</text>
